Sebastian,

How is it possible for a bicycle to have a number of wheels other than two,
and still be a bicycle? It has the prefix "bi".  If it has one wheel, it's
a unicycle. If it has three wheels, it's a tricycle.

I am completely in favor of a Lojban word for a human-powered wheeled
vehicle regardless of the number of wheels, so consider this a friendly
amendment to your proposal.

-Eppcott


